# Dagric OS — make the Dagric profile the terminal's default.
#
# Without this, Dagric.profile is merely one more entry in Settings > Manage
# Profiles that nobody will ever open, and every terminal still launches the
# built-in Breeze profile. This is the line that connects them.
#
# System-level (/etc/xdg, the bottom of KConfig's cascade), NOT skel: an owner
# who picks a different profile in Konsole writes the choice into their own
# ~/.config/konsolerc, which permanently outranks this file. This only decides
# what the machine does before anyone has expressed an opinion. Same placement,
# and the same reasoning, as /etc/xdg/klipperrc and /etc/xdg/ksplashrc.
#
# THE ".profile" SUFFIX IS LOAD-BEARING. ProfileManager::loadAllProfiles picks
# the default with
#   path.endsWith(QLatin1Char('/') + defaultProfileFileName)
# against the full path of each scanned file — so this must be the FILE NAME,
# extension and all. `DefaultProfile=Dagric` matches nothing and is ignored
# without any error.
#
# The group really is [Desktop Entry], despite this not being a .desktop file:
#   KConfigGroup group = m_config->group(QStringLiteral("Desktop Entry"));
#   QString defaultProfileFileName = group.readEntry("DefaultProfile", "");
#
# Safe if it ever goes stale. ProfileManager assigns
# `_defaultProfile = _builtinProfile;` BEFORE reading this key, so a renamed or
# missing profile leaves stock Konsole — an unbranded terminal, never a broken
# one.
#
# This also reaches konsolepart embedders that specify no default of their own
# (Kate's terminal panel), because ProfileManager falls back to reading
# konsolerc for them. That is wanted: the embedded terminal should not be a
# different colour from the standalone one.
[Desktop Entry]
DefaultProfile=Dagric.profile
